      <h3><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">📝</span> Quizzes</h3>

<p>Each unit includes a multiple-choice quiz that tests your understanding of the readings and lesson content. These are <strong>self-study tools</strong> — you'll get instant feedback on your answers so you can see what you've grasped and where you might need to revisit the material.</p>

<h4>What each quiz covers</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quiz 1:</strong> Plato — <em>Euthyphro</em>, <em>Apology</em>, and <em>Crito</em></li>
<li><strong>Quiz 2:</strong> Descartes — <em>Meditations on First Philosophy</em></li>
<li><strong>Quiz 3:</strong> Hume — <em>Enquiry Concerning Human Understanding</em></li>
<li><strong>Quiz 4:</strong> Hegel — <em>Introduction to the Philosophy of History</em></li>
<li><strong>Quiz 5:</strong> Marx — <em>Communist Manifesto</em></li>
<li><strong>Quiz 6:</strong> Sartre — <em>Existentialism Is a Humanism</em></li>
</ul>

<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">💡</span><div class="callout__content">
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Take each quiz after you've finished all the lesson pages and readings for that unit. They're there to help you learn, not to penalize you.</p>
</div></div>
